From: 1582130940 <19632674+1582130940@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: fix RTL826x probe ret declaration

The RTL8261N USXGMII SerDes reset workaround registers a devm cleanup
action from rtl826x_probe() and stores the result in ret, but the probe
local declaration was not added.

Add the missing local variable so the pending patch stack builds until
upstream carries the same fix.

Signed-off-by: 1582130940 <19632674+1582130940@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2606,6 +2606,7 @@ static int rtl826x_probe(struct phy_devi
 {
 	struct device *dev = &phydev->mdio.dev;
 	struct rtl826x_priv *priv;
+	int ret;
 
 	priv = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(struct rtl826x_priv), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!priv)
